  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing a Rights-Based Approach to Return, Readmission and Reintegration in Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia is a host country, country of origin and transit for hundreds of thousands of migrants and returnees traveling mainly along the Eastern and Central Mediterranean Routes intending to reach Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC), mainly the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia (KSA) and Europe respectively. This project contributes to improving a rights-based approach to Return, Readmission and Reintegration, in particular in the target country so returns are better coordinated, managed, and migrants are better protected, assisted and enabled to sustainably reintegrate within their communities, while contributing to the development.</narrative>
  </description>
